C-family operators (diag.invalid_operator_sequence, error): && and || get
the .AND./.OR. replacement, and a bare & or | is simply invalid. The
glued === / !== forms are left out of this input: the formatter rewrites
`1 === 1` to `1 == = 1`, which introduces unexpected_token errors (an
invariant failure, reported separately).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE CheckPair;
	:PARAMETERS bA, bB;
	:DECLARE bOk;
	bOk := bA && bB;
	bOk := bA || bB;
	bOk := bA & bB;
	bOk := bA | bB;
	:RETURN bOk;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE CheckPair;
	:PARAMETERS bA, bB;
	:DECLARE bOk;
	bOk := bA && bB;
	bOk := bA || bB;
	bOk := bA & bB;
	bOk := bA | bB;
	:RETURN bOk;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:12-4:14 error invalid_operator_sequence: SSL uses '.AND.' instead of '&&'
5:12-5:14 error invalid_operator_sequence: SSL uses '.OR.' instead of '||'
6:12-6:13 error invalid_operator_sequence: '&' is not a valid SSL operator
7:12-7:13 error invalid_operator_sequence: '|' is not a valid SSL operator
